onalize  the story in any way and and show  more to all of these characters to you  know both families and um to just not do  what the media did which was kind of  blanket it in in one way you know and  not show the facts or the details behind  it all so  even with this heavy subject matter  there are elements of fantasy throughout  the series and as a result you have a  song and dance number in this with  colton so what was it like to shoot that  how did it feel to perform that song  with him and did you do you get tired of  it when you have to do it as many times  as i would imagine you had to do it oh  you know this i mean this shoot was a  very heavy shoot every day there was  very intense and i think and that was  the one day where i could feel everyone  felt very light like it was a really  that was one very happy day so i would  have continued we had a great time and  colton's um  so  he's he's a singer so he's like  professional and  like musical theater so that was right  in his lane like he was showing me the  ropes and we had a really great time um  i do love this how the show kind of  balances the fantasy with  reality and kind of the the blurred  lines there because i do think  michelle is you know my character she  kind of lives in between  fantasy and reality a lot of the time so  they use that fantasy device to to show  kind of what's going on in in her head  and and how you know the glee of it all  and how  she kind of was casting herself as the  star in these y.a  stories um  which is just  human  dissection you know to think about  how in comparison was it to do that glee  monologue and the song to the mirror i  mean it's it just broke my heart  watching her do that even though you  also it's kind of weird and you also  feel a little uncomfortable  it's still just heartbreaking to watch  that oh man yeah that was the hardest  scene i think i've ever done in my life  right now  up until this point it was  i i had to watch i watched that clip of  lea michelle so many times countless  times i wrote on my legal pad like every  single mannerism that she did at the  time that she did it and when she got  emotional and when she held back when  she would close her eyes and every  gesture was there so i had to  mimic that because michelle was kind of  it was very meta because michelle's  mimicking grief  but she's feeling grief herself and lea  michelle is  you know feeling grief for her real life  boyfriend who passed away but also  acting on a show and mourning the  character that he played on the show so  it's all  there's there's so much going on in that  moment um and i do think  to hold all that together because you  that is the climax of the pilot like you  have to  there's a moment where you you're  feeling for michelle but then i think  you want the audience to wonder if it  was all a dramatization or you know  there's a bit there's something twisted  inside her that she is mimicking  um  grief and trying to  to kind of  put that on of the grieving widow in a  way so um  obviously we explore that more but that  is a you know a taste for the start of  the series just you know the audience  starts to question a bit what her  intentions are you know which we don't  have all the answers to necessarily but  um and we still don't but we are asking  those questions so did you  have conversations about  you know why you thought michelle did  what she did or  just their relationship and the  influence she had over him when these  are two people that  were rarely even together in the same  room  yeah i think that's what was so  fascinating to us we had access to all  of the text messages  so  reading those were very haunting and  very difficult but they weren't i mean  you could see that there were these two  people were so  in a dark place like they were both  reaching out to one another kind of  reaching out to the wrong people like  you just wish that they had never met um  and they didn't bring out the best sides 